🟢 DETAILED FLOW CHART (WITH CONTEXTS)
1️⃣ Packet handed to driver

📍 Context: Process / softirq (NET_TX_SOFTIRQ)

netif_send_skb()
   |
ndo_start_xmit(skb)
   |
cpsw_ndo_start_xmit()


Driver decides TX channel and submits packet.

2️⃣ Descriptor creation & DMA mapping

📍 Context: Same as above

cpdma_chan_submit()
   |
spin_lock(chan->lock)
   |
cpdma_chan_submit_si()
   |
 ├─ dma_map_single()   → get DMA address
 ├─ fill CPDMA descriptor:
 |    - hw_buffer = DMA addr
 |    - hw_len
 |    - hw_mode (OWNER | SOP | EOP)
 |    - sw_token = skb
 |
 └─ __cpdma_chan_submit()
        |
        ├─ if channel idle:
        |     write HDP register
        |
        └─ else:
              chain descriptor


➡️ DMA engine now owns the descriptor

3️⃣ DMA Engine transfers packet

📍 Context: Hardware (no CPU)

CPDMA reads descriptor
   |
Bus transaction (AXI/L3)
   |
Fetch packet from RAM
   |
Push data into MAC TX FIFO
   |
MAC → PHY → Ethernet wire


No copying. No CPU involvement.

4️⃣ DMA finishes TX → Interrupt

📍 Context: HARD IRQ

CPDMA clears OWNER bit
   |
TX interrupt asserted
   |
cpsw_tx_interrupt()


Minimal work only:

cpsw_tx_interrupt()
   |
disable/ack TX IRQ
   |
napi_schedule(&napi_tx)


🚨 No descriptor cleanup here

5️⃣ NAPI scheduled → NET_RX_SOFTIRQ

📍 Context: SOFTIRQ (NET_RX_SOFTIRQ)

NET_RX_SOFTIRQ raised
   |
__do_softirq()
   |
net_rx_action()
   |
napi_poll()

6️⃣ NAPI poll → TX completion

📍 Context: NET_RX_SOFTIRQ

napi_poll()
   |
napi->poll()
   |
cpsw_tx_poll()
   |
cpdma_chan_process()


For each completed TX descriptor:

__cpdma_chan_free()
   |
 ├─ read sw_token (skb)
 ├─ dma_unmap_single()
 ├─ cpdma_desc_free()
 └─ cpsw_tx_handler(skb)

7️⃣ TX handler (driver level)

📍 Context: NET_RX_SOFTIRQ

cpsw_tx_handler()
   |
dev_kfree_skb_any(skb)
   |
update tx stats
   |
netif_tx_wake_queue()


dev_kfree_skb_any() decides where to free:

8️⃣ skb deferred free → NET_TX_SOFTIRQ

📍 Context: SOFTIRQ (NET_TX_SOFTIRQ)

__dev_kfree_skb_irq()
   |
queue skb on completion_queue
   |
raise NET_TX_SOFTIRQ

9️⃣ Final skb destruction

📍 Context: NET_TX_SOFTIRQ

net_tx_action()
   |
process completion_queue
   |
__kfree_skb()
